---
/**
 * index.astro — the wicked-crew landing page (wc.wickedagile.com).
 *
 * POSITIONING (operator, option a): crew is the harness that runs the coding-agent CLIs you
 * already use (Claude Code, Codex, Pi, OpenCode, Copilot) through governed, gated jobs, in
 * sandboxed containers, where every gate says what actually ran; an ungated step reads "approved
 * by default, not verified", so "done" is never claimed past what was checked.
 * It is NOT the skills catalog (that is wicked-garden).
 *
 * Shape (v2, 2026-11-02): ONE job follows you down the page. The hero runs job r-4f2a (intent in →
 * plan → build in a sandbox → review by a different agent, with a dispute a council settles → QE
 * acceptance → a pull request); the next four frames are that job's beats, each with one thing you
 * can explore: Build (the sandbox), Review (the dispute), Gate (the receipt and its labels) and
 * Deliver (workflows as data, a crash and a resume). Then what's new, the family map and Get it.
 * Every interactive region is a fixed box sized for its tallest state (all states stacked in one
 * grid cell), so a hover, a tap or an animation swaps content and never moves its neighbours.
 *
 * ACCURACY (crew main, 2026-11-01), each from README.md / CHANGELOG.md / packages/crew-api-types:
 *  - Sandbox images: Claude Code, Codex, Copilot, OpenCode, Pi. Antigravity's is defined, its seat benched; a local
 *    model or custom binary needs your own image (WICKED_SEAT_IMAGE_<CLI>), offline only. The
 *    worktree is the only repo path mounted writable; the repository boundary is mounted read-only
 *    (wicked-core src/container_floor.rs mount_plan); the model gateway is the only egress; keys
 *    stay in a credential broker, except a Claude subscription seat's sign-in token, which the seat
 *    receives and a guard checks each step's changes and the delivery for (src/seat_secret_guard.rs).
 *  - Gates resolve deny-dominates on the layers that ran (evidence floor, repo checks, policies,
 *    an evaluator on a distinct agent, a judge that can reject but never approve alone). An
 *    ungated phase reads "approved by default, not verified"; a gate with no distinct judge is
 *    "floor only"; a builder reviewing its own work only under explicit "reduced assurance".
 *  - QE acceptance: feature / bug / migration / mcp-server (and editor-plugin) need a QE-ledger
 *    PASS attributed to the run before delivery (409 qe_acceptance_required); CONDITIONAL and a
 *    missing verdict deny. Waivable by the run's lowest-band score, skippable with a reason.
 *  - Councils (operator doctrine D5): convened only to settle a concrete dispute. A reviewer's
 *    finding the builder declines, the reviewer holds, becomes a dispute; a council of N seats
 *    (Settings councilSize 1..9, default 3) drawn at random with a recorded seed rules yes / no /
 *    no_verdict with agreement and dissent, recorded on the receipt (AssuranceReceipt.councils).
 *    Units are routed `teamed` by skills, never by a council (wicked-core#590 S5). After two
 *    send-backs a review_adjudication gate asks the operator.
 *  - Crash: a daemon that dies mid-run resumes the orphaned run at boot (crew#830), re-entering the
 *    unit it was on, audited run.resumed {via: 'boot'}. One machine today; no remote runner.
 *  - Workflows are data: built-ins feature / bug / migration / mcp-server / editor-plugin /
 *    domain-extraction (wicked-core src/catalog.rs); your own is a preset saved with
 *    PUT /api/v1/presets/:name. domain-extraction loops page by page until REAL requirements reach
 *    the minimum (requirementsGraph.minCoveragePct, default 80; placeholders never count).
 *  - Power mode is the default launch for a repo-scoped preset or plan (routes.ts powerModeDefault):
 *    one orchestrator seat builds in checkpointed turns, rigor re-scored from the diff, and the
 *    hand-off runs review / security / QE; a NOT-PASS goes back up to 3 rounds, then asks.
 *  - A NEW failure sends the work back (power hand-off, a send-back) or stops the job; a failure the base
 *    shares is excluded only when the build guide can separate it (repo_checks.rs pass_excluded).
 *  - Repo checks: the repository's own typecheck, lint and tests (build guide, .wicked/checks.json,
 *    or package.json / Cargo.toml), compared with the run's base (wicked-core src/repo_checks.rs).
 *  - Gate labels (studio GateVerdict.tsx): "floor only" = a pass where the floor (incl. the repo
 *    checks) ran and no distinct judge reviewed it; "approved by default, not verified" = nothing
 *    gated the phase. The receipt explorer marks only the layers each label speaks about.
 *  - Needs wicked-garden >= 12.64.0 (the governed-worker base skill and the Apps skill), Node >= 22, a container runtime.
 * The demo is scripted and says so. Never hardcode a version in prose (build-injected stamp only).
 * The words are the reviewed copy (messaging COPY.md rev 5, crew#1260): moved, split and visualized
 * here, never reworded into new claims.
 */
import Base from 'wicked-web/layouts/Base.astro';
import Topbar from 'wicked-web/components/Topbar.astro';
import Footer from 'wicked-web/components/Footer.astro';
import SameGarden from 'wicked-web/components/SameGarden.astro';
import '../styles/crew.css';

// The hook. Two strings, so a variant is a one-line swap.
const HEADLINE = 'The harness for the coding agents you already use.';
const KICKER_IN = 'Intent in.';
const KICKER_OUT = 'Gated work out.';
// The sub-line (the words PR's rendering: the caveat label in plain quotes; the promise carries the weight).
const SUBLINE_A = 'Claude Code, Codex, GitHub Copilot, OpenCode and Pi run your jobs in sandboxes, through gates that';
const SUBLINE_EM = 'say plainly what actually ran';
const SUBLINE_B = '. A step that passed without verification is labelled “approved by default, not verified”.';

const title = 'wicked-crew — the harness for the coding agents you already use';
const description =
  'wicked-crew runs the coding agents you already use (Claude Code, Codex, GitHub Copilot, OpenCode, Pi) through gated jobs in sandboxed containers. Every gate says what actually ran, a different agent reviews the work by default, and the built-in feature, bug-fix, migration, MCP-server and editor-plugin jobs need QE acceptance before delivery (or a labelled waiver or skip). Jobs are durable workflows that resume after a crash, on your own machine and your own plans.';
const repo = 'https://github.com/mikeparcewski/wicked-crew';

const PHASES = ['Plan', 'Build', 'Review', 'QE', 'Deliver'];

// The page's spine: the hero's job, then its four beats.
const BEATS = [
  { id: 'job', name: 'The job' },
  { id: 'build', name: 'Build' },
  { id: 'review', name: 'Review' },
  { id: 'gate', name: 'Gate' },
  { id: 'deliver', name: 'Deliver' },
];

const AGENTS = [
  { name: 'Claude Code', image: 'yes' },
  { name: 'Codex', image: 'yes' },
  { name: 'GitHub Copilot', image: 'yes' },
  { name: 'OpenCode', image: 'yes' },
  { name: 'Pi', image: 'yes' },
  { name: 'Antigravity', image: 'sandbox image defined; the agent is benched for now' },
  { name: 'A local model, or your own binary', image: 'your own image, offline' },
];

// Benefit 1, split: its first sentence leads the Build beat; the rest is the broker's hotspot.
const B1_LEAD = 'By default each runs in a sandbox with no capabilities, a read-only root and one way out: the model gateway (you need a container runtime: Docker, Podman, Rancher Desktop, Colima or OrbStack).';
const B1_BROKER = 'Keys stay in a broker and the sandbox sees placeholders. A Claude subscription’s sign-in token is the one exception: a guard checks each step’s changes and the delivery for it, failing the step or refusing the delivery on a match.';

// The sandbox's four hotspots (benefit 1 and the sandbox facts, placed where they happen).
const HOTS = [
  { key: 'repo', name: 'Your repo', tag: 'read-only', fact: 'Your repo is read-only.' },
  { key: 'worktree', name: 'Worktree + git state', tag: 'writable', fact: 'The job writes its worktree and its git state.' },
  { key: 'gateway', name: 'Model gateway', tag: 'the only way out', fact: 'The model gateway is the only way out.' },
  { key: 'broker', name: 'Broker', tag: 'keys → placeholders, one exception', fact: B1_BROKER },
];

const LAYERS = [
  { key: 'floor', name: 'Evidence check (the floor)', does: 'The job changed its worktree.', can: 'a pass with no judge reads “floor only”' },
  { key: 'checks', name: 'Your checks and policies', does: 'Your repo’s own typecheck, lint and tests, plus the rules you approved.', can: 'a new failure sends it back, waits for you or stops the job' },
  { key: 'eval', name: 'Evaluator', does: 'By default, a different agent reviews the work.', can: 'can send it back' },
  { key: 'judge', name: 'Judge', does: 'An AI judge reads the evidence cold.', can: 'can fail a gate, never approve alone' },
  { key: 'qe', name: 'QE acceptance', does: 'Garden’s QE pipeline, read from the QE ledger; a low-impact change may waive it.', can: 'when required, only an attributed PASS delivers' },
];

const LABELS = [
  { key: 'nogate', label: 'approved by default, not verified', when: 'the phase had no gate' },
  { key: 'floor', label: 'floor only', when: 'no distinct judge could review it' },
  { key: 'reduced', label: 'reduced assurance', when: 'you let the builder review its own work' },
  { key: 'qeskip', label: 'QE acceptance skipped by operator', when: 'you skipped it, with your reason' },
];

const WORKFLOWS = [
  { name: 'feature', steps: 'clarify → design → build → adversarial-review → test → review' },
  { name: 'bug', steps: 'triage → reproduce → fix → verify' },
  { name: 'migration', steps: 'plan → execute → cutover → verify → cleanup' },
  // mcp-server's nine steps (wicked-core src/presets/mcp-server.json) do not fit the frame at
  // 1280x660, so it keeps the words PR's one line, with no step counter
  { name: 'mcp-server', steps: 'build an MCP server, install it on consent' },
  // exactly the steps of wicked-core src/presets/editor-plugin.json (main ca90345); install asks first
  { name: 'editor-plugin', steps: 'scope → design → build → test → security-review → install-plan → install' },
  // not a fixed sequence of steps: one line, and no step counter
  { name: 'domain-extraction', steps: 'cover code with real requirements (default 80%)' },
];
// A workflow's steps as rail nodes: the arrows separate steps; a one-line description is one node.
const stepsOf = (s: string) => s.split('→').map((x) => x.trim());

// The dispute, step by step (the council proof's flow, with the demo job's own lines).
const DISPUTE = [
  { name: 'Finding', what: 'The reviewer flags a problem, with the file and line.', job: 'Codex finding (high): the limit is keyed on IP; the brief says per API key · rateLimit.ts:12' },
  { name: 'Declined', what: 'The builder disagrees and says why.', job: 'Claude Code declines: “IP is right for routes with no key”' },
  { name: 'Held', what: 'The reviewer stands by it. Now it is a dispute.', job: 'Codex holds the finding → dispute' },
  { name: 'Council', what: 'Three agents, drawn at random with a recorded seed, rule on it.', job: 'council convened: 3 of 4 eligible agents, seed 4127 · Pi, OpenCode, Copilot' },
  { name: 'Ruling', what: 'Yes, no, or no verdict, with the agreement and the dissent.', job: 'council ruled: finding stands · 2 of 3 · OpenCode dissented' },
];

// Benefit 2, the reviewed words split into its three cases (one row each), not reworded.
const BENEFIT_2 = {
  h: 'A failed check sends work back, waits for you or stops the job.',
  rows: [
    { k: 'Power mode', note: 'a preset or plan launched on a repository; on by default', p: 'the code-writing step runs as one agent’s checkpointed turns; a failed review or a qualifying build-check failure goes back to the builder, up to three hand-off attempts in all; problems that need your judgment pause for you.' },
    { k: 'Phased job', note: '', p: 'retries, escalates or stops.' },
    { k: 'No other agent can review', note: '', p: 'the job stops unless you launch it as “reduced assurance”, which is labelled (a saved workflow may require fewer checks; its requirements are listed in the receipts).' },
  ],
};
const BENEFIT_3 = {
  h: 'Tested before delivery, with receipts.',
  p: 'Jobs launched as a feature, bug fix, migration, MCP server or editor plugin pass QE acceptance first, unless a labelled waiver or skip says otherwise; a plan you compose yourself, a build continued from a chat, or a saved workflow that does not ask for it, requires none. Every gate says plainly what a pass means: what it checked, and what was waived or skipped.',
};

// What's new (crew 0.16.11 and 0.16.12), one line each.
const NEW = [
  { name: 'Power mode', line: 'On by default when a preset or a plan is launched on a repository; the code-writing step runs as one agent’s checkpointed turns, its rigor re-scored from the diff.' },
  { name: 'Proposed learnings', line: 'Jobs can propose new learnings for your approval, each with its source job and who proposed it.' },
  { name: 'Requirements graphs', line: 'Counted against a minimum; placeholders never count.' },
  { name: 'Voice', line: 'Transcription on your machine (whisper.cpp, installed separately); the audio is never stored.' },
  { name: '“Check on it?”', line: 'A different agent reads a long step’s record and recommends; if none can, crew gives its own labelled reading. It changes nothing.' },
  { name: 'Sandbox images', line: 'On Docker, protected from the runtime’s automatic cleanup; a missing built-in image is rebuilt on next use, and Nerve Center shows their state.' },
];

// Injected at build time from packages/crew/package.json via astro.config.mjs (DT-7).
const crewVersion = __WICKED_CREW_VERSION__;
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Topbar pkg="wicked-crew" repo={repo} />
  <!-- Frames rise in as they arrive. Set before the first frame paints, so nothing flashes; if the
       page script never runs, the switch is taken back off and everything simply shows. -->
  <script is:inline>(function(){try{if(window.matchMedia&&matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches)return;var h=document.documentElement;h.classList.add('can-rise');setTimeout(function(){if(!window.__crewArrive)h.classList.remove('can-rise');},3000);}catch(e){}})();</script>

  <!-- The spine, at 1024px wide and up: job r-4f2a's five beats as one thread under the topbar,
       filling as each beat arrives (decoration; the beat kickers and the gutter track say it in words). -->
  <div class="thread" data-thread aria-hidden="true">{BEATS.map((b) => <i data-thread-seg={b.id}><b></b></i>)}</div>

  <!-- The spine: job r-4f2a's beats, in the right gutter (1400px wide and up only). -->
  <nav class="beats" data-beats aria-label="Job r-4f2a, beat by beat">
    <ol>
      {BEATS.map((b, i) => (
        <li><a href={`#${b.id}`} data-beat-link={b.id}><span class="beats-l">{b.name}</span><span class="beats-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="sr-only">{`, beat ${i + 1} of 5`}</span></a></li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </nav>

  <!-- ── S1 · Hook + the job demo ───────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="frame hero" id="job" data-frame data-beat="job" aria-labelledby="hero-h">
    <div class="hero-glow" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="wrap hero-head">
      <p class="hero-kicker"><span class="kick-in">{KICKER_IN}</span> <span class="kick-out">{KICKER_OUT}</span></p>
      <h1 id="hero-h">{HEADLINE}</h1>
      <p class="lede">{SUBLINE_A} <strong>{SUBLINE_EM}</strong>{SUBLINE_B}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="job" data-job aria-label="A working demo: one job through its gates">
        <div class="job-bar">
          <span class="job-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
          <span class="job-t">job r-4f2a · <b>feature</b> · phased</span>
          <span class="job-note">scripted demo</span>
          <span class="job-acts">
            <button type="button" class="job-btn job-btn--go" data-job-run><span class="lbl stack"><span class="stack-i is-on" data-l="go">Run the job</span><span class="stack-i" data-l="again" aria-hidden="true">Run it again</span></span></button>
            <button type="button" class="job-btn job-btn--kill" data-job-kill aria-disabled="true"><span class="lbl stack"><span class="stack-i is-on" data-l="kill">Kill the daemon</span><span class="stack-i" data-l="start" aria-hidden="true">Start the daemon</span></span></button>
          </span>
          <a class="job-install" href="#get">Install</a>
        </div>
        <div class="track-wrap">
          <p class="io io--in"><small>{KICKER_IN}</small>{' '}<span>add rate limiting to the public API</span></p>
          <div class="track-mid">
            <ol class="track" data-track aria-label="Phases and their gates">
              {PHASES.map((p, i) => (
                <li class="st" data-st={i}>
                  <span class="st-name">{p}</span>
                  <button type="button" class="st-gate" data-gate={i} aria-disabled="true" aria-pressed="false" aria-label={`${p} gate receipt`}>gate</button>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ol>
            <div class="rail" aria-hidden="true"><i data-rail></i></div>
          </div>
          <p class="io io--out" data-pr><small>{KICKER_OUT}</small>{' '}<span>pull request #42</span></p>
        </div>
        <div class="job-body">
          <div class="log-col">
            <div class="log" data-log role="log" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Job events"></div>
            <p class="caption" data-caption><span class="caption-n" data-caption-n></span><span data-caption-t></span></p>
          </div>
          <aside class="panel" data-panel tabindex="-1" aria-live="polite" aria-label="Gate receipt or decision"></aside>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── S2 · Build: your agents, sandboxed ─────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="frame sec build" id="build" data-frame data-beat="build" aria-labelledby="sandbox-h">
    <div class="wrap two two--build">
      <div class="sec-copy">
        <p class="beat"><span class="beat-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="beat-id">job r-4f2a ·</span> Build</p>
        <h2 id="sandbox-h">Your agents, sandboxed.</h2>
        <p class="lead">{B1_LEAD}</p>
        <p class="sub">crew drives each agent’s own headless mode in a hardened sandbox, on your accounts and plans.</p>
        <p class="pull">Your accounts, your plans: no billing, no reselling.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="sbx" data-sbx>
        <div class="sbx-map" role="group" aria-label="What the sandbox can reach">
          {HOTS.filter((h) => h.key !== 'worktree').map((h) => (
            <button type="button" class={`hot hot--${h.key}`} data-hot={h.key} aria-pressed={h.key === 'broker' ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-controls="sbx-cap">
              <b>{h.name}</b>{' '}<small>{h.tag}</small>
            </button>
          ))}
          <div class="sbx-box">
            <span class="sbx-tag" aria-hidden="true">sandbox</span>
            <span class="sbx-agent"><i class="sbx-pulse" aria-hidden="true"></i><span data-sbx-agent>Claude Code</span></span>
            {HOTS.filter((h) => h.key === 'worktree').map((h) => (
              <button type="button" class={`hot hot--${h.key}`} data-hot={h.key} aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="sbx-cap">
                <b>{h.name}</b>{' '}<small>{h.tag}</small>
              </button>
            ))}
          </div>
          <span class="wire wire--ro" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
          <span class="wire wire--out" aria-hidden="true"><i class="pkt"></i></span>
          <span class="wire wire--keys" aria-hidden="true"><i></i></span>
        </div>
        <div class="sbx-cap stack" id="sbx-cap" aria-live="polite">
          {HOTS.map((h) => (
            <p class:list={['stack-i', { 'is-on': h.key === 'broker' }]} data-cap={h.key}><b>{h.name}</b>{' '}<span>{h.fact}</span></p>
          ))}
          {AGENTS.map((a, i) => (
            <p class="stack-i" data-cap={`agent-${i}`}><b>{a.name}</b>{' '}<span class:list={['sbx-img', { 'is-yes': a.image === 'yes' }]}>{a.image === 'yes' ? 'sandbox image ships with crew; you sign in with your own account' : a.image}</span></p>
          ))}
        </div>
        <div class="agents" role="group" aria-label="Pick an agent to put in the sandbox">
          {AGENTS.map((a, i) => (
            <button type="button" class:list={['agent', { 'is-yes': a.image === 'yes' }]} data-agent={i} data-agent-name={a.name} aria-pressed={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-controls="sbx-cap">{a.name}</button>
          ))}
        </div>
        <p class="sbx-note">Sign each agent in once, on the Agents page of studio, the browser UI that ships inside crew.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── S3 · Review: a different agent, and a council for disputes ─────── -->
  <section class="frame sec review" id="review" data-frame data-beat="review" aria-labelledby="council-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head">
        <p class="beat"><span class="beat-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i></i><i></i></span><span class="beat-id">job r-4f2a ·</span> Review</p>
        <h2 id="council-h">A council settles disputes. It doesn’t pick agents.</h2>
        <p class="sub">By default a different agent reviews the work. Agents are routed by their skills; a council is convened only when a reviewer and a builder disagree about a finding.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="two two--review">
        <div class="benefit benefit--rows">
          <h3>{BENEFIT_2.h}</h3>
          <dl class="cases">
            {BENEFIT_2.rows.map((r) => (
              <div class="case"><dt><b>{r.k}</b>{r.note && <Fragment>{' '}<span class="case-note">({r.note})</span></Fragment>}:</dt>{' '}<dd>{r.p}</dd></div>
            ))}
          </dl>
        </div>
        <div class="disp" data-disp>
          <ol class="disp-steps" aria-label="How a dispute reaches a council">
            {DISPUTE.map((d, i) => (
              <li><button type="button" class="disp-step" data-dstep={i} aria-controls="disp-stage" aria-current={i === 0 ? 'step' : undefined}><span class="disp-n">{i + 1}</span>{' '}<b>{d.name}</b></button></li>
            ))}
          </ol>
          <div class="disp-stage stack" id="disp-stage" aria-live="polite">
            {DISPUTE.map((d, i) => (
              <div class:list={['stack-i', 'disp-card', { 'is-on': i === 0 }]} data-dpanel={i}>
                <p class="disp-what"><b>{d.name}</b>{' '}<span>{d.what}</span></p>
                <p class="disp-job">{d.job}</p>
                {i === 3 && (
                  <p class="disp-seats" aria-label="4 eligible agents; 3 drawn">
                    <span class="seat-chip on">Pi</span> <span class="seat-chip on">OpenCode</span> <span class="seat-chip on">Copilot</span> <span class="seat-chip">not drawn</span> <span class="seed">seed 4127</span>
                  </p>
                )}
                {i === 4 && (
                  <p class="disp-seats"><span class="vote yes">Pi · stands</span> <span class="vote yes">Copilot · stands</span> <span class="vote no">OpenCode · dissent</span> <span class="seed">sent back to Build with the ruling</span></p>
                )}
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="disp-ctl">
            <button type="button" class="ctl-btn" data-dprev aria-label="Previous step">← Prev</button>
            <button type="button" class="ctl-btn" data-dnext aria-label="Next step">Next →</button>
            <button type="button" class="ctl-btn" data-dreplay>Replay</button>
            <span class="disp-count mono" data-dcount aria-hidden="true">1 / 5</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="facts facts--row" role="list">
        <li>The ruling is on the gate’s receipt.</li>
        <li>Council size is a setting: 1 to 9, default 3.</li>
        <li>In a phased job, after two send-backs, the job asks you instead.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── S4 · Gate: every gate says what it checked ─────────────────────── -->
  <section class="frame sec gate" id="gate" data-frame data-beat="gate" aria-labelledby="gates-h">
    <div class="wrap two two--gate">
      <div class="sec-copy">
        <p class="beat"><span class="beat-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i></i></span><span class="beat-id">job r-4f2a ·</span> Gate</p>
        <h2 id="gates-h">Every gate says what it checked.</h2>
        <p class="sub">A gate decides on the layers that actually ran. A new failure sends the work back, waits for you or stops the job, and no model can approve on its own.</p>
        <div class="benefit">
          <h3>{BENEFIT_3.h}</h3>
          <p>{BENEFIT_3.p}</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rcx" data-rcx>
        <p class="rcx-k">Pick a receipt. When a gate is weaker than a full pass, it says so:</p>
        <ul class="labels rcx-pick" role="list">
          <li><button type="button" class="rcx-opt rcx-opt--full" data-scen="full" aria-pressed="true" aria-controls="rcx-card"><b>PASS</b>{' '}<span>every layer ran</span></button></li>
          {LABELS.map((l) => (
            <li><button type="button" class="rcx-opt" data-scen={l.key} aria-pressed="false" aria-controls="rcx-card"><b>{l.label}</b>{' '}<span>{l.when}</span></button></li>
          ))}
        </ul>
        <div class="rcx-card" id="rcx-card">
          <div class="rcx-head">
            <span class="rcx-title">Gate receipt · <span class="nw">r-4f2a</span>
              <span class="rcx-when stack" aria-hidden="true">
                <span class="stack-i is-on" data-when="full">every layer ran</span>
                {LABELS.map((l) => <Fragment>{' '}<span class="stack-i" data-when={l.key}>{l.when}</span></Fragment>)}
              </span>
            </span>
            <span class="rcx-stamp stack" aria-live="polite">
              <span class="stack-i is-on ok" data-stamp="full">PASS</span>
              {LABELS.map((l) => <Fragment>{' '}<span class="stack-i" data-stamp={l.key}>{l.label}</span></Fragment>)}
            </span>
          </div>
          <table class="tbl tbl--layers rcx-layers">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Layer</th><th scope="col">On this receipt</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {LAYERS.map((l, i) => (
                <tr data-layer={l.key}>
                  <th scope="row"><button type="button" class="rcx-l" data-layer-btn={l.key} aria-pressed={i === 2 ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-controls="rcx-detail">{l.name}</button></th>
                  <td><span class="rcx-s" data-s={l.key}>ran</span></td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <div class="rcx-detail stack" id="rcx-detail" aria-live="polite">
            {LAYERS.map((l, i) => (
              <dl class:list={['stack-i', { 'is-on': i === 2 }]} data-detail={l.key}>
                <div><dt>What it checks</dt><dd>{l.does}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Its power</dt><dd>{l.can}</dd></div>
              </dl>
            ))}
            <dl class="stack-i" data-detail="nogate">
              <div><dt>What it checks</dt><dd>Nothing: no gate ran on this phase.</dd></div>
              <div><dt>Its power</dt><dd>none: the step passes, labelled “approved by default, not verified”</dd></div>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── S5 · Deliver: workflows are data, jobs survive a crash ─────────── -->
  <section class="frame sec deliver" id="deliver" data-frame data-beat="deliver" aria-labelledby="durable-h">
    <div class="wrap two two--deliver">
      <div class="sec-copy">
        <p class="beat"><span class="beat-dots" aria-hidden="true"><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i><i class="on"></i></span><span class="beat-id">job r-4f2a ·</span> Deliver</p>
        <h2 id="durable-h">Workflows are data. Jobs survive a crash.</h2>
        <p class="end-line">r-4f2a ends as pull request #42, with its evidence bundle ready to export.</p>
        <p class="sub">Pick a built-in, or save your own steps as a preset (<code>PUT /api/v1/presets/:name</code>).</p>
        <div class="wf" data-wf>
          <div class="wf-tabs" role="group" aria-label="Built-in workflows">
            {WORKFLOWS.map((w, i) => (
              <button type="button" class="wf-tab" data-wf-tab={i} aria-pressed={i === 0 ? 'true' : 'false'} aria-controls="wf-stage"><code>{w.name}</code></button>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="wf-stage stack" id="wf-stage">
            {WORKFLOWS.map((w, i) => (
              <ol class:list={['stack-i', 'wf-rail', { 'is-on': i === 0, 'is-single': !w.steps.includes('→') }]} data-wf-panel={i} aria-label={`${w.name}: ${w.steps}`}>
                {stepsOf(w.steps).map((s) => <li class="wf-node" data-node><span class="wf-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="wf-s">{s}</span></li>)}
              </ol>
            ))}
          </div>
          <div class="wf-ctl">
            <button type="button" class="ctl-btn ctl-btn--deny" data-wf-crash><span class="lbl stack"><span class="stack-i is-on" data-l="crash">Crash it</span><span class="stack-i" data-l="start" aria-hidden="true">Start the daemon</span></span></button>
            <p class="wf-status" data-wf-status aria-live="polite">running</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="facts facts--cards" role="list">
        <li><b>Power mode by default.</b> For a preset or plan on a repo; see Review. The job above is shown phased, one gate per step.</li>
        <li><b>Crash-resumable.</b> A daemon that dies mid-job resumes it at boot, at the step it was on.</li>
        <li><b>One open API.</b> Studio ships inside crew and uses the same <code>/api/v1</code> and <code>/ws</code> your tools can.</li>
        <li><b>Headless too.</b> <code>wicked-crew start</code>, the REST API, or <code>wicked-crew mcp</code> for agents.</li>
        <li><b>One machine today.</b> A remote runner is the direction, not a shipped feature.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ── S6 · What's new (after the proofs) ─────────────────────────────── -->
  <section class="frame sec news" id="news" data-frame aria-labelledby="news-h">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="sec-head news-head">
        <h2 id="news-h">What’s new.</h2>
        <div class="car-ctl" data-car-ctl>
          <button type="button" class="ctl-btn" data-car-prev aria-label="Previous release note">←</button>
          <span class="car-count mono" data-car-count aria-live="polite">1 of 6</span>
          <button type="button" class="ctl-btn" data-car-next aria-label="Next release note">→</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <ul class="news-list" data-news role="list">
        {NEW.map((n, i) => (
          <li style={`--i:${i}`}><span class="news-n mono" aria-hidden="true">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>{' '}<b>{n.name}</b>{' '}<span>{n.line}</span></li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <div class="car-dots" data-car-dots aria-hidden="true">{NEW.map(() => <i></i>)}</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <SameGarden current="wicked-crew" />

  <!-- ── S8 · Get it ───────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
  <div class="finale">
    <section class="frame get" id="get" data-frame>
      <div class="wrap get-grid">
        <div class="get-intro">
          <h2>Install it with the family. Studio comes with it.</h2>
          <ul class="needs" role="list">
            <li>Node 22 or later</li>
            <li>A container runtime: Docker, Podman, Rancher Desktop, Colima or OrbStack</li>
            <li>wicked-garden 12.64.0 or later, for the skills every agent follows</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="get-tos">
            <b>Terms of service:</b> crew drives CLIs you installed under your own accounts. Check
            that each one’s terms allow programmatic use.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="install-stack">
          <div class="install install--primary" role="group" aria-label="Install with the wicked family installer">
            <div class="install__bar">
              <span class="install__label"><span class="install__star" aria-hidden="true">★</span> Recommended · family installer</span>
              <button class="install__copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy family installer command"
                onclick="navigator.clipboard&&navigator.clipboard.writeText('npx wicked-installer').then(()=>{this.textContent='Copied';setTimeout(()=>{this.textContent='Copy';},1400);})">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <pre class="install__code"><code><span class="type" data-type>npx wicked-installer</span>   <span class="c"># picks crew, garden and the rest</span></code></pre>
            <p class="install__note">Installs crew and garden together. <span class="install__ver">wicked-crew npm v{crewVersion}</span></p>
          </div>

          <div class="install-or" aria-hidden="true"><span>or install just crew</span></div>

          <div class="install install--secondary" role="group" aria-label="Install wicked-crew directly">
            <div class="install__bar">
              <span class="install__label">Direct · wicked-crew only</span>
              <button class="install__copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy direct install commands"
                onclick="navigator.clipboard&&navigator.clipboard.writeText('npm install -g wicked-crew\nwicked-crew serve').then(()=>{this.textContent='Copied';setTimeout(()=>{this.textContent='Copy';},1400);})">Copy</button>
            </div>
            <pre class="install__code"><code>npm install -g wicked-crew
wicked-crew serve   <span class="c"># opens studio on 127.0.0.1:7701</span></code></pre>
          </div>
        </div>
        <a class="gh-pill" href="https://github.com/mikeparcewski/wicked-crew#readme" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="View wicked-crew on GitHub">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="42" height="42" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.02-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82a7.6 7.6 0 0 1 2-.27c.68 0 1.36.09 2 .27 1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.01 8.01 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z"/></svg>
          <span>View on GitHub</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Footer repo={repo} />
  </div>

  <script>
    import '../scripts/job-demo.js';
    import '../scripts/explore.js';
    import '../scripts/settle.js';
    import '../scripts/arrive.js';
  </script>
</Base>
